	"notes": "Django's documentation page uses the oldest trick in the book — CSS float — to put the article on the left and a small donate box on the right. What is worth noticing is that this split is fluid, not fixed: the scan shows the same roughly 69/31 share of the row on a laptop, a desktop and a giant ultrawide screen, so a wider monitor gives both columns more room rather than just adding empty margin. On a phone the nav bar hides behind a menu button and the donate box moves underneath the article, turning the page into one column. Above the two-column body sit two full-width colour bands — a warning and a promo — that have nothing to do with the columns below them, and below it is a plain five-column footer of links.",
